{
 "about": "Slot pools for frames (W1) and transition families (W2). A text names a pool as {name}; the generator draws one value per pool per item from the seed, so a slot used twice repeats the same value. The need and the clue must hold for every value in a pool, so a frame relies only on what is true of the whole pool. researcher and artist are made-up full names, used once: refer back with 'the researcher', 'the team', 'the artist', never a pronoun or a surname alone. science_field, social_field and art_form are bare lowercase nouns that take a singular verb. animals and plants are plural common names. dig_site and field_site carry their article ('a hilltop fort in Wales'); field_site is a land site with soil and plants. early_period (before about 1500) and modern_period (1800s-1900s) carry 'the' or a possessive and read after 'in' or 'during'. artwork takes 'the' or a possessive ('the mural of dockworkers at dawn', \"{artist}'s mural...\"). small_percent is under 10 percent, large_percent a clear majority, sample_size a count of people or things, study_year a year from 1985 on. Do not combine a site or a period with another site, period, animals or plants in one text. Only researcher, artist and study_year may start a sentence. Fixed excerpt frames (with source) use no slots.",
